		<label>Type 63-1</label>
		<description>Caliber: 7.62x39mm. 20-round detachable mag. Select-Fire.
		
The Type 63 is a Chinese assault rifle designed in the 1960s. The rifle is externally very similar to the Type 56 SKS, but uses the rotating-bolt system taken off of the Kalashnikov-derived Type 56 AK. Type 63s were originally intended to replace both the AK and SKS-type rifles in service, and the initial production weapons were promising. However, the main production versions suffered from numerous quality control issues, and while the Type 63 did enter service, it only served as a secondary weapon and was phased out during the late 1970s - well before either weapon it was supposed to replace.

The Type 63-1 variant is a rarer version that features an underfolding stock.</description>
